2:T6ff,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a Mutual Consent Divorce take to complete in Family Court?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A mutual consent divorce (Sec 13B HMA) generally takes around 6 months between the 1st Motion and 2nd Motion, though courts may waive the 6-month period under specific circumstances."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is monthly maintenance calculated in family disputes? (भरण-पोषण कैसे तय होता है?)","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Under Section 125 CrPC / BNSS, courts evaluate the income of both spouses, standard of living during marriage, financial liabilities, and reasonable needs of the dependent spouse and minor children."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What factors determine child custody in a divorce case?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Child custody is decided based on the overall welfare and best interests of the child, considering the child’s age, educational background, emotional bonding, and living environment offered by each parent."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where are matrimonial and divorce petitions filed in Roorkee?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Matrimonial suits, maintenance petitions, and divorce applications arising in Roorkee are filed before the Family Court having jurisdiction over Roorkee and Haridwar district."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Stridhan and how can a woman claim it back?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Stridhan includes all gifts, jewelry, cash, and items presented to a woman before, during, or after marriage. It is her exclusive property, and a petition under Section 406 IPC / DV Act can be filed for its recovery."}}]}0:{"buildId":"FH8UeKfY7251wkI4fw6lu","rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"page-animate","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema